# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env* is gitignored; this template is not.
#
# Local development: `pnpm db:start`, then `pnpm db:status` prints
# these. They are identical on every local install, so they are not secrets.
#
# Hosted project: Settings -> API Keys.
#
# Use the **publishable key** (`sb_publishable_…`). It replaced the legacy `anon`
# JWT, which still works but is being retired, and it can be rotated without
# reissuing tokens.
#
# The **secret key** (`sb_secret_…`, formerly service_role) is deliberately not
# listed and must never be added. It bypasses every row-level security policy,
# and this app reaches Postgres directly from the browser — the whole security
# model rests on no code path holding that key. See docs/architecture.md.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
